Looking at the code, I can see the bug: in `parseVC5()` at lines 385-387, when an optional tag is detected (tag with 0x8000 bit set), the code attempts to strip the optional bit by negating the tag:

```cpp
bool optional = matches(tag, VC5Tag::Optional);
if (optional)
  tag = -tag;
```

This negation doesn't correctly strip the optional bit. Instead of `tag & ~Optional`, it produces incorrect values. Let me create a VC5 input to trigger this issue.

